<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH IPB TO LOWER BASE RATE TO 21.5 PCT FROM WED.</title>
<headline>CZECH IPB TO LOWER BASE RATE TO 21.5 PCT FROM WED.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>IPB a.s., the Czech Republic's third largest bank, said on Tuesday that it would lower its base lending rate for new credits by one full percentage point to 21.5 percent, effective July 2.</p>
</text>
